Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Eric

I'm afraid all I can do is empathise with you.  You cannot have two types of stratification (geographic and object-level) in the same analysis; the software can't cope.

As you noted, by employing a non-equal coverage probability design between your geographic strata, your analysis must respect that stratification criterion. Your low sampling intensity in the low density geographic stratum has conspired to defeat your ability to analyse the low density stratum alone.

Perhaps others more clever than I have a solution, but I don't.

